# Build-context hygiene for the Docker build (T055) — first Java service to
# add this (discovery-service/T028, connection-service/T034 and
# rating-service/T046 all deferred it). Maven's own build output
# (target/, the Java equivalent of .NET's bin/obj/) and local IDE/wrapper
# cache noise have no reason to ride along in the build context: the
# Dockerfile's build stage runs its own `./mvnw package` from source inside
# the container, so a host machine's stale target/ directory should never
# be copied in and silently shadow what that stage produces.
target/
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
# The wrapper jar itself is fetched fresh by mvnw on first use inside the
# build stage — shipping a host-cached copy in the build context is just
# dead weight, not a correctness risk, but it's still noise worth excluding.
.mvn/wrapper/*.jar
